 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Brown bread, cheese, crackers, apple sauce, and nuts are all compact and easy to eat on the go. A baguette and some cheese can keep you going for that distance. Fill up on on trail water stations and carry a small water bottle if you start to feel thirsty. A bag of mix nuts and dried fruit makes a great pick me up without the gushy feeling. If you think you might want to share food with friends, it' worth having a few light bowls. Otherwise, keep the bowls to snacks you can eat with one hand.",
